_ROUTE";s:9:"API Route";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.API_ROUTE_HELP";s:26:"The base route for the API";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.VERSION_PREFIX";s:14:"Version Prefix";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.VERSION_PREFIX_HELP";s:26:"Current API version prefix";s:18:"PLUGIN_API.BACKEND";s:7:"Backend";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.FLEX_PAGES_BACKEND";s:18:"Flex Pages Backend";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.FLEX_PAGES_BACKEND_HELP";s:77:"Use Flex-Objects for page listings (faster search, filtering, and pagination)";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.FLEX_ACCOUNTS_BACKEND";s:21:"Flex Accounts Backend";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.FLEX_ACCOUNTS_BACKEND_HELP";s:65:"Use Flex-Objects for user listings (faster search and pagination)";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.KEEP_CACHE_FOR_API_REQUESTS";s:27:"Keep Cache for API Requests";s:43:"PLUGIN_API.KEEP_CACHE_FOR_API_REQUESTS_HELP";s:353:"Keep Grav's object cache on for API requests even when the global cache is turned off. Disabling the cache is a frontend-dev convenience (to see template changes live), but the API renders no frontend pages — so leaving this on keeps the admin fast while the frontend runs uncached. Turn off only if you need the API to honor the global cache setting.";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.AUTHENTICATION";s:14:"Authentication";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.API_KEY_AUTHENTICATION";s:22:"API Key Authentication";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_AUTHENTICATION";s:18:"JWT Authentication";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY";s:23:"JWT Access Token Expiry";s:39:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY_HELP";s:32:"Access token lifetime in seconds";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY";s:24:"JWT Refresh Token Expiry";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY_HELP";s:33:"Refresh token lifetime in seconds";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_SIGNING_ALGORITHM";s:21:"JWT Signing Algorithm";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.JWT_SIGNING_ALGORITHM_HELP";s:209:"HMAC algorithm used to sign and verify API tokens. Only symmetric HS variants are supported because tokens are signed with a single shared secret. Leave on HS256 unless you have a specific reason to change it.";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.SESSION_AUTHENTICATION";s:22:"Session Authentication";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.SESSION_AUTHENTICATION_HELP";s:47:"Allow existing admin sessions to access the API";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.API_KEY_VERIFICATION_CACHE";s:26:"API Key Verification Cache";s:42:"PLUGIN_API.API_KEY_VERIFICATION_CACHE_HELP";s:213:"How long (seconds) to remember a verified API key so repeat requests skip the deliberately-slow bcrypt check. Revoking, disabling or expiring a key still takes effect immediately. Set to 0 to verify every request.";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.RELEASE_SESSION_LOCK_EARLY";s:26:"Release Session Lock Early";s:42:"PLUGIN_API.RELEASE_SESSION_LOCK_EARLY_HELP";s:234:"Commit the session right after authentication on read-only (GET) requests so the new admin's parallel calls don't queue behind PHP's per-session file lock. Recommended on. Turn off only if a custom read endpoint writes to the session.";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.PROTECT_FRONTEND_SESSION";s:25:"Protect Front-end Session";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.PROTECT_FRONTEND_SESSION_HELP";s:345:"Keep API calls from touching the public site's session. Calls made with a token or API key and no session cookie skip the PHP session entirely, and any other call that arrives without its own session cookie never plants a new one. This stops the API from booting a visitor who is logged in to the public site in the same browser. Recommended on.";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.TRANSLATION_OVERRIDES";s:21:"Translation Overrides";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.TRANSLATION_OVERRIDES_HELP";s:206:"Apply the translation overrides stored in user/languages so they also beat the active theme's own strings. Turning this off leaves the files in place but stops them overriding theme wording. Recommended on.";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOW_DRAFT_PREVIEW";s:19:"Allow Draft Preview";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOW_DRAFT_PREVIEW_HELP";s:241:"Let the new admin's page editor preview an unpublished page on the front end. The preview is authorized by a short-lived token minted only for users who can read the page, so turning this off disables draft previews entirely. Recommended on.";s:24:"PLUGIN_API.LOGIN_CAPTCHA";s:13:"Login Captcha";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.LOGIN_CAPTCHA_HELP";s:168:"Require a captcha challenge on the admin login form. The login is already rate-limited and supports per-account 2FA, so this is an extra layer rather than the only one.";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTCHA_PROVIDER";s:16:"Captcha Provider";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTCHA_PROVIDER_HELP";s:186:"Cap is a proof-of-work challenge served by this plugin — no keys and no third-party service. Turnstile and reCAPTCHA require the Form plugin, and use the keys already configured there.";s:23:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTCHA_MODE";s:12:"Captcha Mode";s:28:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTCHA_MODE_HELP";s:131:"Invisible solves in the background while the user types their credentials. Checkbox makes them click. Honored by Cap and Turnstile.";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.GUARD_LOGIN";s:11:"Guard Login";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.GUARD_FORGOTTEN_PASSWORD";s:24:"Guard Forgotten Password";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.GUARD_FORGOTTEN_PASSWORD_HELP";s:118:"Recommended — the forgotten-password endpoint sends mail, which makes it a more attractive target than login itself.";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.GUARD_FIRST_RUN_SETUP";s:21:"Guard First-run Setup";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.GUARD_FIRST_RUN_SETUP_HELP";s:46:"Only reachable on a site with no accounts yet.";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.CAP_DIFFICULTY";s:14:"Cap Difficulty";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.CAP_DIFFICULTY_HELP";s:149:"Leading zero bits each sub-challenge must produce. Higher is more work for the client — raise only if you are seeing scripted attempts get through.";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.CAP_SUB_CHALLENGES";s:18:"Cap Sub-challenges";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.CAP_SUB_CHALLENGES_HELP";s:94:"How many sub-challenges make up one captcha. The default takes well under a second on a phone.";s:15:"PLUGIN_API.CORS";s:4:"CORS";s:24:"PLUGIN_API.CORS_SETTINGS";s:13:"CORS Settings";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.ENABLE_CORS";s:11:"Enable CORS";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOWED_ORIGINS";s:15:"Allowed Origins";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOWED_ORIGINS_HELP";s:262:"Exact origins (scheme + host) allowed to call the API from a browser, e.g. https://app.example.com. Empty means same-origin only. Avoid "*": it lets any website read authenticated responses, so a configured wildcard is honored only for unauthenticated endpoints.";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOWED_METHODS";s:15:"Allowed Methods";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOWED_METHODS_HELP";s:38:"HTTP methods allowed for CORS requests";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.ALLOWED_HEADERS";s:15:"Allowed Headers";s:24:"PLUGIN_API.RATE_LIMITING";s:13:"Rate Limiting";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.ENABLE_RATE_LIMITING";s:20:"Enable Rate Limiting";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW";s:19:"Requests Per Window";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW_HELP";s:42:"Maximum number of requests per time window";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.TIME_WINDOW";s:11:"Time Window";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.TIME_WINDOW_HELP";s:28:"Rate limit window in seconds";s:18:"PLUGIN_API.CONTENT";s:7:"Content";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.MEDIA_METADATA";s:14:"Media Metadata";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.MAXIMUM_VALUE_LENGTH";s:20:"Maximum Value Length";s:36:"PLUGIN_API.MAXIMUM_VALUE_LENGTH_HELP";s:149:"Longest metadata value (characters) accepted when saving. Values are also stripped of HTML tags, since they render into image attributes on the site.";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.EDITABLE_METADATA_FIELDS";s:24:"Editable Metadata Fields";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.EDITABLE_METADATA_FIELDS_HELP";s:321:"Descriptive fields shown in the media metadata editor. The key is written verbatim into the .meta.yaml sidecar. A field can be single-line text, multi-line text, a tag list, a select dropdown, a number, a date (YYYY-MM-DD) or a true/false toggle. Any other keys (EXIF, dimensions, upload info) are left untouched on save.";s:14:"PLUGIN_API.KEY";s:3:"Key";s:19:"PLUGIN_API.KEY_HELP";s:87:"Sidecar key, e.g. alt, title, caption. Letters, numbers, dot, dash and underscore only.";s:16:"PLUGIN_API.LABEL";s:5:"Label";s:21:"PLUGIN_API.FIELD_TYPE";s:10:"Field Type";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.SINGLE_LINE";s:11:"Single line";s:21:"PLUGIN_API.MULTI_LINE";s:10:"Multi-line";s:20:"PLUGIN_API.TAGS_LIST";s:11:"Tags (list)";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.SELECT_LIST";s:17:"Select (dropdown)";s:17:"PLUGIN_API.NUMBER";s:6:"Number";s:15:"PLUGIN_API.DATE";s:17:"Date (YYYY-MM-DD)";s:18:"PLUGIN_API.BOOLEAN";s:20:"Boolean (true/false)";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.SELECT_OPTIONS";s:7:"Options";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.SELECT_OPTIONS_HELP";s:97:"Only used by Select fields: the value stored in the sidecar, and the label shown in the dropdown.";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.SELECT_OPTION_VALUE";s:12:"Stored value";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.SELECT_OPTION_LABEL";s:5:"Label";s:21:"PLUGIN_API.NUMBER_MIN";s:7:"Minimum";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.NUMBER_MIN_HELP";s:84:"Only used by Number fields: the smallest accepted value. Leave empty for no minimum.";s:21:"PLUGIN_API.NUMBER_MAX";s:7:"Maximum";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.NUMBER_MAX_HELP";s:83:"Only used by Number fields: the largest accepted value. Leave empty for no maximum.";s:19:"PLUGIN_API.REQUIRED";s:8:"Required";s:24:"PLUGIN_API.REQUIRED_HELP";s:87:"A save can't leave this field empty. Clearing all of a file's metadata still clears it.";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.PAGE_STATISTICS";s:15:"Page Statistics";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.TRACK_PAGE_VIEWS";s:16:"Track Page Views";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.TRACK_PAGE_VIEWS_HELP";s:60:"Record frontend page views for the Page Statistics dashboard";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDE_LOGGED_IN_ADMINS";s:24:"Exclude Logged-in Admins";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDE_LOGGED_IN_ADMINS_HELP";s:113:"Skip page views made while logged in with admin access, so your own testing and demo visits do not skew the stats";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDED_IP_ADDRESSES";s:21:"Excluded IP Addresses";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDED_IP_ADDRESSES_HELP";s:122:"Visitor IPs or CIDR ranges to exclude from tracking, e.g. 203.0.113.7 or 203.0.113.0/24. IPv4 and IPv6 are both supported.";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDE_NON_BROWSER_CLIENTS";s:27:"Exclude Non-Browser Clients";s:43:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDE_NON_BROWSER_CLIENTS_HELP";s:237:"Skip page views from command-line and library HTTP clients such as curl, wget, Go-http-client and python-requests. These report themselves as browsers rather than bots, so a scanner hitting your site would otherwise count as real traffic";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDED_USER_AGENTS";s:20:"Excluded User Agents";s:36:"PLUGIN_API.EXCLUDED_USER_AGENTS_HELP";s:173:"Additional User-Agent fragments to exclude from tracking, matched anywhere in the header and ignoring case, e.g. uptimerobot or my-scanner. Added to the built-in list above.";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.AUDIT_TRAIL";s:11:"Audit Trail";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.ENABLE_AUDIT_TRAIL";s:18:"Enable Audit Trail";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.ENABLE_AUDIT_TRAIL_HELP";s:156:"Record API activity (logins, content, user, config, and package changes) to a queryable log shown under Tools. Visible to super admins only. Off by default.";s:23:"PLUGIN_API.DETAIL_LEVEL";s:12:"Detail Level";s:28:"PLUGIN_API.DETAIL_LEVEL_HELP";s:146:"Standard records who did what, when, and from where. Detailed additionally captures field-level before/after values for page edits (more storage).";s:25:"PLUGIN_API.RETENTION_DAYS";s:16:"Retention (days)";s:30:"PLUGIN_API.RETENTION_DAYS_HELP";s:91:"Automatically delete entries older than this many days. Set 0 to keep entries indefinitely.";s:26:"PLUGIN_API.MAXIMUM_ENTRIES";s:15:"Maximum Entries";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.MAXIMUM_ENTRIES_HELP";s:83:"Hard cap on stored entries; the oldest are trimmed once exceeded. Set 0 for no cap.";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.ANONYMIZE_IP_ADDRESSES";s:22:"Anonymize IP Addresses";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.ANONYMIZE_IP_ADDRESSES_HELP";s:162:"Mask the last part of each IP before storing (last octet for IPv4, last 80 bits for IPv6), for GDPR-friendlier logs. Off keeps full addresses for forensic detail.";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_AUTHENTICATION";s:22:"Capture Authentication";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_AUTHENTICATION_HELP";s:51:"Logins, failed logins, logouts, and password resets";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_CONTENT_CHANGES";s:23:"Capture Content Changes";s:39:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_CONTENT_CHANGES_HELP";s:48:"Page create, update, delete, move, and translate";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_MEDIA_CHANGES";s:21:"Capture Media Changes";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_MEDIA_CHANGES_HELP";s:27:"Media uploads and deletions";s:37:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_USER_GROUP_CHANGES";s:28:"Capture User & Group Changes";s:42:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_USER_GROUP_CHANGES_HELP";s:41:"User and group create, update, and delete";s:40:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_CONFIGURATION_CHANGES";s:29:"Capture Configuration Changes";s:45:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_CONFIGURATION_CHANGES_HELP";s:39:"System and plugin configuration updates";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_PACKAGE_CHANGES";s:23:"Capture Package Changes";s:39:"PLUGIN_API.CAPTURE_PACKAGE_CHANGES_HELP";s:59:"Plugin and theme install, update, remove, and Grav upgrades";s:20:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_MODE";s:9:"Demo Mode";s:22:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_NOTICE";s:430:"Demo mode is turned on **per account**, by giving an account the *Demo Mode* permission (`access.api.demo`). A demo account can look at everything but can only change what you allow below, and server paths, logs and backups are hidden from it. Save the starting state and reset to it from the **Set Baseline / Reset Now** panel, or with `bin/plugin api demo:baseline`, `bin/plugin api demo:reset` and `bin/plugin api demo:status`.";s:29:"PLUGIN_API.WRITABLE_RESOURCES";s:17:"Demo accounts may";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.WRITABLE_RESOURCES_HELP";s:189:"Leave empty for a read-only demo. Users, packages, system tools, backups, webhooks, the system and security settings, and the API, Admin, Login and Email plugin settings are always refused.";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_PAGES_CREATE";s:12:"Create pages";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_PAGES_UPDATE";s:10:"Edit pages";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_PAGES_DELETE";s:12:"Delete pages";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_MEDIA_UPLOAD";s:12:"Upload media";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_MEDIA_UPDATE";s:18:"Edit media details";s:34:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_MEDIA_DELETE";s:12:"Delete media";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_CONFIG_SITE";s:20:"Change site settings";s:36:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_CONFIG_PLUGINS";s:22:"Change plugin settings";s:35:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_CONFIG_THEMES";s:21:"Change theme settings";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_PAGES_ALL";s:19:"Everything on pages";s:31:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_MEDIA_ALL";s:19:"Everything on media";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_GRANT_CONFIG_ALL";s:31:"Site, plugin and theme settings";s:28:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_ALLOW_ROUTES";s:12:"Extra routes";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_ALLOW_ROUTES_HELP";s:179:"Other API routes a demo account may write to, such as a plugin's own. Write <code>METHOD /path</code> or <code>/path</code>, below the API prefix; <code>*</code> matches anything.";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_ESCAPE_HTML";s:17:"Show HTML as text";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_ESCAPE_HTML_HELP";s:155:"Pages a demo account saves show their raw HTML as text, so visitors cannot add scripts or hidden links. Demo accounts can never save a page that runs Twig.";s:28:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_INCLUDE_CODE";s:24:"Reset plugins and themes";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_INCLUDE_CODE_HELP";s:88:"Also restore user/plugins and user/themes on every reset. Symlinked ones are left alone.";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_EXTRA_ROOTS";s:10:"Also reset";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.DEMO_EXTRA_ROOTS_HELP";s:134:"More <code>user://</code> folders to restore on every reset, such as <code>user://data</code> for what visitors do on the site itself.";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_INTERVAL_MINUTES";s:24:"Reset Interval (minutes)";s:38:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_INTERVAL_MINUTES_HELP";s:102:"How often demo content resets back to the captured baseline. Only takes effect once a baseline exists.";s:27:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_ON_REQUEST";s:23:"Reset On Request (Lazy)";s:32:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_ON_REQUEST_HELP";s:147:"Reset opportunistically on incoming API requests when the content is stale. Recommended for installs that do not run `bin/grav scheduler` via cron.";s:28:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_ON_SCHEDULE";s:17:"Reset On Schedule";s:33:"PLUGIN_API.RESET_ON_SCHEDULE_HELP";s:83:"Also register a Scheduler job, for installs that run `bin/grav scheduler` via cron.";s:37: